                <pb facs="0727" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/856: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-05T12:00:00+00:00">December 5,
                        1919—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5557. For the Secretary of State from Polk: Your 3942 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >3941</hi>], December 2, 4 p.m. Arrangements have been made with General
                    Connor for holding the <hi rendition="#italic">America</hi>. Mission will leave
                    Paris in accordance with your instructions on the evening of the 9th, and we
                    hope to sail from Brest on the 10th. Polk.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
